From d0df438c6074b93dcbea1f571208f5c9347a73c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/52] Place text in KiCad schematic SVG exports like KiCad
 does

Text went through TextMixin.to_svg(), whose rotation and mirror handling
differs from KiCad's. It swaps the alignment of text at 180 degrees, so
labels at (at x y 180) with (justify right), the way KiCad saves every
label pointing left, were drawn on the wrong side of their wire. Fields
of mirrored and rotated symbols ended up in the wrong place, and pin
numbers were drawn at the inner end of the pin instead of its middle.

Instead, follow KiCad's own code for each kind of text:

- Symbol fields: KiCad lays out the field's box in the symbol's
  untransformed frame, transforms its center with the symbol, and draws
  the text centered there, horizontal or vertical depending on the
  field's and the symbol's rotation.
- Free text, local, global and hierarchical labels: KiCad derives a spin
  style from the angle and justification, and keeps text upright.
- Pin names and numbers: inside the body after the pin name offset, or
  above and below the middle of the pin when the offset is 0.
- Sheet pins.

Text is drawn with KiCad's metrics: the stroke font's space width, its
line pitch for multi-line text, KiCad's gap between text and wires and
its pen widths. KiCad's text escapes, such as {slash} in net names, are
resolved like KiCad's UnescapeString() does.

